        "title": "The Five Canons of Rhetoric",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The five canons are the organizational framework of the complete rhetorical task: from finding what to say (inventio) through delivering it effectively (actio). They originated in Roman rhetoric (Cicero's De Inventione, the Rhetorica ad Herennium) and remained the curriculum of rhetoric for 1,500 years. Each canon is a distinct dimension of the communication challenge."
